  "title": "Selection's hub composes the knot's emergence as a 2-sum",
  "subject": "Whether the emergence that the pieces of a knot's space keep after a line is removed survives across the 3-edge cuts along which the pieces are glued",
  "conclusion": "Removing a line from a knot's space ties its three points into a hub, exactly the point side of the 3-edge cuts along which the space is spliced from Fano atoms and planar glue. After any removal off a cut's point side the hub holds one bit, and by the knot's symmetry under complementing every value the knots crossing the cut are exactly the 2-sums of a circuit through the hub on each side.",
